  "findings": [
    "CommandReturn#executeArg creates an ordinary Message using reversed participants, inherited dotted ArrowConfiguration, optional return COLOR override, and owned deactivation. Rust resolves contexts then replaces Return events in a cloned diagram and reruns render. Each restart removes Return events and preserves indices; no unbounded same-event recursion was found. The previously panicking valid self-return cases now render, and eight fresh ordinary recursion/order/label cases pass across both engines.",
    "Fresh checker_recovery_colored_teoz0 and colored_teoz1 fail. The parser stores #purple as part of ReturnMessage.label; lowering at sequence.rs:7625 clones the original arrow and never consumes the return color. Java applies withColor and excludes the color token from label width. Example legacy self return canvas is321px in Java versus374px in Rust. This is a parser-to-lowering dependency, not a font or frontend discrepancy.",
    "Two deliberate orphan-return controls are rejected by raw Java (exit200 with error SVG) while Rust returns exit0 with an SVG. They remain negative controls, never counted as positive parity. Lowered self arrows also inherit the reversed-direction and attached-note component failures recorded below.",
    "All14 accounts were present byte-for-byte in earlier chronological commits before their corresponding code. See provenance.json and commit-mapping.json. Main release tiers remain11181/11251 product-library and10497/11251 assisted-library; source-only CLI cohort403/955 with10 invalid references; no regressions observed.",
    "Verdict applies to whole source-to-SVG recovery with the dependencies described above. Positive component-local observations are explicitly bounded and are not acceptance. Every mismatch and negative remains in the standing suite."
  ],
